return {h=9,w=100,cr=255,hc=5,bh=70,gr="slow",eg={"water2","dragon"},st={20,10,55,15,20,80},ab={{33,0},{155,1}},genus={en="Fish Pokémon",es="Pokémon Pez",pt="Pokémon Peixe"},flavor={en={[1]="In the distant past, it was somewhat stronger than the horribly weak descendants that exist today.",[2]="In the distant past, it was somewhat stronger than the horribly weak descendants that exist today.",[3]="Famous for being very unreliable. It can be found swimming in seas, lakes, rivers and shallow puddles.",[4]="An underpowered, pathetic Pokémon. It may jump high on rare occasions, but never more than seven feet.",[5]="For no reason, it jumps and splashes about, making it easy for predators like PIDGEOTTO to catch it mid-jump.",[6]="This weak and pathetic Pokémon gets easily pushed along rivers when there are strong currents.",[7]="MAGIKARP is a pathetic excuse for a Pokémon that is only capable of flopping and splashing. This behavior prompted scientists to undertake research into it.",[8]="MAGIKARP is virtually useless in battle as it can only splash around. As a result, it is considered to be weak. However, it is actually a very hardy Pokémon that can survive in any body of water no matter how polluted it is.",[9]="Its swimming muscles are weak, so it is easily washed away by currents. In places where water pools, you can see many MAGIKARP deposited there by the flow.",[10]="It is virtually worthless in terms of both power and speed. It is the most weak and pathetic Pokémon in the world.",[11]="In the distant past, it was somewhat stronger than the horribly weak descendants that exist today.",[12]="It is said to be the world’s weakest Pokémon. No one knows why it has managed to survive.",[13]="It is unable to swim against even slow-moving currents. It always splashes about for some reason.",[14]="A MAGIKARP living for many years can leap a mountain using Splash. The move remains useless, though.",[15]="An underpowered, pathetic Pokémon. It may jump high on rare occasions, but usually not more than seven feet.",[16]="For no reason, it jumps and splashes about, making it easy for predators like PIDGEOTTO to catch it mid-jump.",[17]="A Magikarp living for many years can leap a mountain using Splash. The move remains useless, though.",[18]="A Magikarp living for many years can leap a mountain using Splash. The move remains useless, though.",[21]="A Magikarp living for many years can leap a mountain using Splash. The move remains useless, though.",[22]="A Magikarp living for many years can leap a mountain using Splash. The move remains useless, though.",[23]="It is virtually worthless in terms of both power and speed. It is the most weak and pathetic Pokémon in the world.",[24]="In the distant past, it was somewhat stronger than the horribly weak descendants that exist today.",[25]="Magikarp is a pathetic excuse for a Pokémon that is only capable of flopping and splashing. This behavior prompted scientists to undertake research into it.",[26]="Magikarp is virtually useless in battle as it can only splash around. As a result, it is considered to be weak. However, it is actually a very hardy Pokémon that can survive in any body of water no matter how polluted it is.",[27]="Although weak and helpless, this Pokémon is incredibly fertile. They exist in such multitudes, you’ll soon grow tired of seeing them.",[28]="Its reckless leaps make it easy pickings for predators. On the bright side, many Pokémon enjoy longer life spans, thanks to Magikarp.",[29]="In the distant past, they were fairly strong, but they have become gradually weaker over time.",[30]="Thanks to their strong hold on life, dirty water doesn’t bother them at all. They live in waters all over the world!",[31]="Famous for being very unreliable. It can be found swimming in seas, lakes, rivers, and shallow puddles.",[32]="Famous for being very unreliable. It can be found swimming in seas, lakes, rivers, and shallow puddles.",[33]="It is virtually worthless in terms of both power and speed. It is the most weak and pathetic Pokémon in the world.",[34]="This weak and pathetic Pokémon gets easily pushed along rivers when there are strong currents.",[39]="A feeble, pitiful imbecile of a Pokémon that is nonetheless very hardy. Unperturbed by turbid water, it can be found living in all sorts of places."},es={[23]="No es precisamente rápido ni fuerte. Es el Pokémon más debilucho y simplón de todos los que hay.",[24]="En un pasado lejano, era más fuerte de lo que hoy son sus débiles descendientes.",[25]="Magikarp es el triste ejemplo de un Pokémon capaz únicamente de saltar y salpicar. Esta conducta llevó a científicos a estudiarlo en profundidad.",[26]="Magikarp es prácticamente inútil en combate; solo sirve para salpicar, y se le considera muy débil. Con todo, en realidad es un Pokémon muy resistente. Sobrevive en cualquier medio acuático, aunque esté contaminado.",[27]="Es muy débil y de poca utilidad, aunque su capacidad reproductora resulta abrumadora. Lo normal es encontrar Magikarp por doquier.",[28]="Como lo único que hace es chapotear en el agua, resulta una presa fácil. Gracias a esto, muchos otros Pokémon pueden sobrevivir.",[29]="Al parecer, en la antigüedad había gozado de gran fuerza, pero con el paso del tiempo se ha ido debilitando hasta su estado actual.",[30]="Su resistencia le permite vivir en las aguas más turbias. Por eso se los puede ver nadando en cualquier lugar del mundo.",[31]="Famoso por su ineptitud. Nada en todo tipo de aguas, ya sean mares, lagos, ríos o charcas.",[32]="Famoso por su ineptitud. Nada en todo tipo de aguas, ya sean mares, lagos, ríos o charcas.",[33]="Es el Pokémon más débil y patético que existe, con una fuerza y velocidad prácticamente nulas.",[34]="Este Pokémon débil y patético se limita a dejarse llevar por la corriente cuando esta tiene fuerza."},pt="Um Pokémon fraco, patético e tolo, mas muito resistente. Como a água turva não o incomoda, pode ser encontrado vivendo em todo tipo de lugar."},evo={{s=1